Z||000000||JoeFiero||10-22-2001||08:36 PM||||I am in need of a new engine for my '87 coupe, it is in great condition but overheated and broke a rod.  I was looking at rebuiltengines.com , does anyone have other suggestions?<P>Thanks,<P>FieroJoe||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-22-2001||10:30 PM||||nice name!<P><BR>PM FieroMaster88, he might still have his for sale.  engine was an 88, has about 35k on it, ran great, would be plug and play into any 87 or 88 Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-23-2001||07:44 AM||||Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory does engine swaps.  He gets remanufactured engines for the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-23-2001||08:21 PM||||87+ Grand Am and Olds Cutlass Calais are two sources. I'd just find a good used motor. they aren't hard to come by. <P>Do some "basic" things for reliability, like replace the cam gear set while it's out and easy to get to. same for the belt tensioner and water pump.<P>Unless you are planning performance work of some type I wouldn't spend allot of money to rebuild one unless it was my only choice. $200-300 used, plus the parts I mention above, vs. $1000+ for a rebuilt that will also likely need aditional items... Just not worth it. (Rebuilts may or maynot come with the belt tensioner, water pump, and other things. Depends where you get them.)<P>If you look around you can often find these motors with only 60,000-80,000miles on them. With new cam gears the odds are good it won't have any problems for another 100,000 or more. (Unless you cook it again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
